{
  "sheet": "voice",
  "about": "Deadlock voice lines (dialogue only, read from the player's install like every other sound; never shown on the pages). group: the line's files in the VPK, sounds/vo/<group>_NN.vsnd (every numbered take is extracted and one is picked at random). trigger: select = the hero's body starts a stage (run start and after every teleport); unselect = the teleporter finishes charging; skill = the skill row (or the ult equipment's row) starts, spoken by the hero the row belongs to, so an ult item used by anyone speaks with its own hero's voice; multikill = the player's hero kills at least `kills` enemies with gaps under 1.5 s (the highest reached plays once per burst); idle = the hero has said nothing for 2-5 min (random). chance: probability the line plays when triggered. gap: seconds since the hero's last line before this one may play (keeps abilities from chattering). One line at a time per hero; lines don't overlap. chain: seconds the line keeps going, a new take starting as soon as the last one ends, in a shuffled order that carries on across uses (no take repeats until every one has played); 0 = one line. skipTakes: Deadlock take numbers (the NN of <group>_NN) left out, comma-separated, or none. Rat King: Deadlock's Rat Swarm lines name his rats (ratking_use_power1, ~125 takes); the creator (2026-10-21) wanted those named ones called out one after another through Royal Pestments, so its row chains them for 6 s, skipping the five that name no rat (106, 111, 114, 116, 117). Deadlock's numbering: use_power1 = Rat Swarm, 2 = Scrap Grenade, 3 = Royal Pestments, 4 = Rule, Ratannia!.",
  "columns": [
    "id",
    "hero",
    "trigger",
    "skill",
    "kills",
    "group",
    "chance",
    "gap",
    "chain",
    "skipTakes"
  ],
